# Agent & LLM Execution Rules

Whenever an AI Agent or LLM CLI (`agy`, Antigravity, Cursor, Copilot, etc.) works on VersionGate, it MUST follow these 8 mandatory rules:

1. Check Existing Files First: Inspect existing utilities, services, repositories, and components before writing new helper code.
2. Solid & Clean Architecture: Enforce modularity (Repositories -> Services -> Controllers -> Routes), strict TypeScript types, and zero symptom-masking.
3. Verification Suite: Always run verification commands before declaring success:
   - `bun run typecheck` (`bunx tsc --noEmit`)
   - `bun run build:dashboard`
   - `bun test --pass-with-no-tests`
4. Semantic Commits: Use Conventional Commits (`feat(...)`, `fix(...)`, `perf(...)`, `ci(...)`, `refactor(...)`, `chore(...)`).
5. Feature Branching & Single PR per Milestone: Work on one feature branch (`feat/*`) per milestone. Group full-stack changes into atomic commits. Do NOT create micro-PRs for minor edits. Open one single PR per milestone assigned to `dineshkorukonda` with proper labels (`enhancement`, `backend`, `frontend`, `infrastructure`, `database`, `bug`).
6. Automated Issue Linking: Every PR body MUST include GitHub keywords to auto-close resolved issues (`Closes #123`, `Fixes #124`, `Resolves #125`).
7. Strict No-Emoji & No-Icon Rule: ABSOLUTELY NO EMOJIS OR DECORATIVE ICON SYMBOLS anywhere across the repository (code, markdown, UI, docs, commit messages). Use clean badges (`[ OK ]`, `01 //`) and typography.
8. Landing Page & Interactive Website Changelog Sync: Every material feature or architectural upgrade MUST update both `website/src/components/capability-grid.tsx` and the interactive changelog page `website/src/app/changelog/page.tsx`.
